BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Bloomington Libraries
DTSTART:20260618T180000Z
DTEND:20260618T190000Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
SUMMARY:Pollinator Week Pop-up Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators and the plants that they help sustain are crucial
  parts of our environment\, in Bloomington and all over the world. Come l
 earn about these amazing creatures with us and celebrate Indiana Universi
 ty's Bee Campus USA designation and Bloomington's Bee City USA designatio
 n!  Page through historical materials from the Lilly Library's collection
 s\, including sumptuously illustrated herbals and medieval books\, waterc
 olor nature diaries\, original photographs by Frank Hohenberger\, and muc
 h more! Or try your hand at some pollinator-themed puzzles with our Curat
 or of Puzzles.  Representatives from the Wylie House Museum will be on ha
 nd to talk about how to plant your own garden to enjoy. Take home some se
 eds for native Indiana plants and learn about the Wylie House heirloom ga
 rden.  And if you're feeling creative\, learn how to make a simple nature
  diary to document your own adventures outside.  This event is free and o
 pen to the public. Stop in any time between 2 and 4 p.m.  For more visito
 r information\, including accessibility and parking information\, please 
 visit the Lilly Library website (https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-libr
 ary/visit).  To stay in the loop about Lilly Library events and exhibitio
 ns\, subscribe to our mailing list (https://go.iu.edulilly-news).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Pollinators and the plants that they he
 lp sustain are crucial parts of our environment\, in Bloomington and all 
 over the world. Come learn about these amazing creatures with us and cele
 brate Indiana University's Bee Campus USA designation and Bloomington's B
 ee City USA designation!</p><p>  Page through historical materials from t
 he Lilly Library's collections\, including sumptuously illustrated herbal
 s and medieval books\, watercolor nature diaries\, original photographs b
 y Frank Hohenberger\, and much more! Or try your hand at some pollinator-
 themed puzzles with our Curator of Puzzles.</p><p>  Representatives from 
 the Wylie House Museum will be on hand to talk about how to plant your ow
 n garden to enjoy. Take home some seeds for native Indiana plants and lea
 rn about the Wylie House heirloom garden.</p><p>  And if you're feeling c
 reative\, learn how to make a simple nature diary to document your own ad
 ventures outside.</p><p>  This event is free and open to the public. Stop
  in any time between 2 and 4 p.m.</p><hr /><p>  For more visitor informat
 ion\, including accessibility and parking information\, please <a href="h
 ttps://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/visit" target="_blank" rel="no
 opener">visit the Lilly Library website</a>.</p><p>  To stay in the loop 
 about Lilly Library events and exhibitions\, <a href="https://go.iu.eduli
 lly-news" target="_blank" rel="noopener">subscribe to our mailing list</a
 >.</p>
UID:20260618T180000Z-2281733@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260428T120846Z
